# Hoisting.
#
# The create-supa-app template ships `node-linker=hoisted`, which builds a
# single flat node_modules at the workspace root and no per-package ones. That
# contradicts @supa-media/testing's reactResolution guardrail, which requires
# react to resolve from apps/mobile's OWN node_modules — so a freshly
# scaffolded app fails its own guardrail on the first install.
# See Supa-Media/supa-framework#49.
#
# This is togather's configuration, which satisfies the guardrail and carries
# the production mileage (and the native-graph lessons in its ADR-013). The
# guardrail is not busywork: when Metro resolves React from the workspace root
# instead of the project root you get "use is not a function" at runtime, on a
# device, with a green CI.
public-hoist-pattern[]=*eslint*
public-hoist-pattern[]=*prettier*
public-hoist-pattern[]=@jest/*
shamefully-hoist=true

# @supa-media/* are published to GitHub Packages.
# GITHUB_TOKEN must be set in the environment (CI: secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN;
# local: `gh auth token`).
@supa-media:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${GITHUB_TOKEN}
